### ==================================================================
### BOOK SERIES
### ==================================================================

### Create a book series
POST http://localhost:8080/api/book-series
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "The Wandering Inn",
  "author": "pirateaba",
  "totalVolumes": null
}

> {%
    client.global.set("wanderingInnSeriesId", response.body.id);
%}

### Get all book series
GET http://localhost:8080/api/book-series

### Get the series just created
GET http://localhost:8080/api/book-series/{{wanderingInnSeriesId}}

### Get a series that doesn't exist -> expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/book-series/999

### Update the series -> every field changed from creation, not just totalVolumes, to actually exercise
### every setter (see the missing setArtist bug caught on the LightNovel vertical: a PUT test that reuses
### creation-time values can pass even though a setter is silently broken)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/book-series/{{wanderingInnSeriesId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "The Wandering Inn (edited)",
  "author": "pirateaba (edited)",
  "totalVolumes": 12
}

### Update a series that doesn't exist -> expect 404
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/book-series/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Doesn't matter",
  "author": "Doesn't matter",
  "totalVolumes": 1
}

### Create with blank name and author -> expect 400 with fieldError map
POST http://localhost:8080/api/book-series
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "author": "",
  "totalVolumes": 1
}

### Delete the series
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/book-series/{{wanderingInnSeriesId}}

### Get the deleted series -> expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/book-series/{{wanderingInnSeriesId}}


### ==================================================================
### BOOK
### ==================================================================

### Create a fresh series for the book tests below
POST http://localhost:8080/api/book-series
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Mistborn",
  "author": "Brandon Sanderson",
  "totalVolumes": 3
}

> {%
    client.global.set("mistbornSeriesId", response.body.id);
%}

### Create a standalone book (no series)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Project Hail Mary",
  "author": "Andy Weir",
  "synopsis": "A lone astronaut must save the earth from disaster.",
  "coverImageUrl": null,
  "publishedDate": "2021-05-04",
  "totalChapters": 46,
  "volumeNumber": null,
  "genres": ["SCIENCE_FICTION"],
  "totalPages": 496
}

> {%
    client.global.set("hailMaryBookId", response.body.id);
%}

### Create a book attached to the series above
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books?seriesId={{mistbornSeriesId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Final Empire",
  "author": "Brandon Sanderson",
  "synopsis": "A young thief discovers she has the power to overthrow an immortal emperor.",
  "coverImageUrl": null,
  "publishedDate": "2006-07-17",
  "totalChapters": 44,
  "volumeNumber": 1,
  "genres": ["FANTASY"],
  "totalPages": 541
}

> {%
    client.global.set("finalEmpireBookId", response.body.id);
%}

### Get all books
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books

### Get the standalone book -> series should be null
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/{{hailMaryBookId}}

### Get the series-linked book -> series should be populated
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/{{finalEmpireBookId}}

### Get a book that doesn't exist -> expect 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/999

### Create a book with a non-existent seriesId -> expect 404 (BookSeriesNotFoundException)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books?seriesId=999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Doesn't matter",
  "author": "Doesn't matter"
}

### Create a book with blank title and author -> expect 400 with fieldError map
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "author": ""
}

### Create a book with a negative totalPages -> expect 400 (validation runs on @Positive fields too)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Doesn't matter",
  "author": "Doesn't matter",
  "totalPages": -5
}

### Try to attach to a series via a nested JSON object instead of ?seriesId= -> expect 201 with series: null
### (id/series are @JsonProperty(access = READ_ONLY): Jackson ignores both on the way in, so this can neither
### spoof an existing row's id nor bypass the BookSeriesNotFoundException check that ?seriesId= goes through)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 999999,
  "title": "Should Not Get A Series",
  "author": "Doesn't matter",
  "series": {"id": 999}
}

> {%
    client.global.set("jsonBypassBookId", response.body.id);
%}

### Confirm the book above got a real server-assigned id (not 999999) and no series attached
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/{{jsonBypassBookId}}

### Clean up the bypass-test book
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/{{jsonBypassBookId}}

### Update the standalone book, attaching it to the series too -> every field deliberately changed from
### creation (not just volumeNumber), to actually exercise every setter (see the missing setArtist bug
### caught on the LightNovel vertical: a PUT test that reuses creation-time values can pass even though a
### setter is silently broken)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/books/{{hailMaryBookId}}?seriesId={{mistbornSeriesId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Project Hail Mary (edited)",
  "author": "Andy Weir (edited)",
  "synopsis": "A lone astronaut wakes up with no memory and must save the earth from disaster.",
  "coverImageUrl": "https://covers.example.com/project-hail-mary.jpg",
  "publishedDate": "2021-05-11",
  "totalChapters": 48,
  "volumeNumber": 2,
  "genres": ["SCIENCE_FICTION", "SURVIVAL"],
  "totalPages": 504
}

### Update a book that doesn't exist -> expect 404
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/books/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Doesn't matter",
  "author": "Doesn't matter"
}

### Try deleting the series while books still reference it -> expect the RESTRICT FK to kick in (409)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/book-series/{{mistbornSeriesId}}

### Delete both books
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/{{hailMaryBookId}}

### Delete the other book
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/books/{{finalEmpireBookId}}

### Now nothing references the series -> delete should succeed this time
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/book-series/{{mistbornSeriesId}}


### ==================================================================
### USER BOOK (tracking)
### ==================================================================

### Register a dedicated user for the tracking tests below, so this file can run standalone
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "book-tracker",
  "password": "supersecret",
  "email": "book-tracker@example.com"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("bookTrackerUserId", response.body.id);
%}

### Create a fresh standalone book to track
POST http://localhost:8080/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "The Way of Kings",
  "author": "Brandon Sanderson",
  "synopsis": "A war-torn world of stone and storms where honor is dying.",
  "coverImageUrl": null,
  "publishedDate": "2010-08-31",
  "totalChapters": 92,
  "volumeNumber": null,
  "genres": ["FANTASY"],
  "totalPages": 1007
}

> {%
    client.global.set("wayOfKingsBookId", response.body.id);
%}

### Start tracking the book above
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/books/{{wayOfKingsBookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "READING",
  "rating": null,
  "currentChapter": 5,
  "currentPage": 120
}

> {%
    client.global.set("userBookWorkId", response.body.id);
%}

### List the READING tab -> should include the tracking record just created
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works?status=READING

### List the FINISHED tab -> should be empty
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works?status=FINISHED

### Track the same book again for the same user -> expect 409 (DuplicateTrackingException)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/books/{{wayOfKingsBookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "READING",
  "rating": null,
  "currentChapter": 1,
  "currentPage": 1
}

### Track for a user that doesn't exist -> expect 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/999/books/{{wayOfKingsBookId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PLAN_TO_READ"
}

### Track a book that doesn't exist -> expect 404
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/books/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "PLAN_TO_READ"
}

### Update progress only -> status/rating should stay untouched
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userBookWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentChapter": 8,
  "currentPage": 200
}

### Update just the rating -> chapter/page from above should be unaffected
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userBookWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 9
}

### Update the status -> currentChapter/currentPage/rating from above should be unaffected; also the first
### test in this file to actually exercise UserWorkController applying request.status()
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userBookWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "FINISHED"
}

### Update with an out-of-range rating -> expect 400 (validation runs on PATCH too)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userBookWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 15
}

### Update with a negative currentPage -> expect 400 (UserWorkUpdateRequest has its own @Positive, PATCH
### binds to the DTO, not the entity, so the entity-side annotation alone would not catch this)
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userBookWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPage": -1
}

### Register a second user, to test the ownership check
POST http://localhost:8080/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "book-tracker-2",
  "password": "supersecret",
  "email": "book-tracker-2@example.com"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("otherBookTrackerUserId", response.body.id);
%}

### Try updating user 1's tracking record through user 2's path -> expect 404, not 200
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{otherBookTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userBookWorkId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 1
}

### Update a user-work that doesn't exist -> expect 404
PATCH http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "rating": 5
}

### Stop tracking -> expect 204
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works/{{userBookWorkId}}

### Confirm it's gone -> READING tab should be empty again
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/{{bookTrackerUserId}}/user-works?status=READING
